          <TD vAlign=3Dtop>
            <H2>Top Ten Cool New Features of Java 2SE 1.4</H2>by <A=20
            href=3D"http://www.onjava.com/pub/au/156">David =
Flanagan</A>, author=20
            of <A href=3D"http://www.oreilly.com/catalog/javanut4/">Java =
in a=20
            Nutshell, 4th Edition</A><BR>03/06/2002 =
</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>
      <P>Java 1.4 has just been released. This is a major new release, =
with 62=20
      percent more classes and interfaces than Java 1.3; needless to =
say, there=20
      are lots of new features. This article describes my personal =
favorite top=20
      ten new features, ordered from cool to extremely cool. You can =
learn more=20
      about all of these features in the 4th edition of <A=20
      href=3D"http://www.oreilly.com/catalog/javanut4/"><I>Java in a=20
      Nutshell</I></A>. Note that the new features I've selected for =
this=20
      article are drawn from those documented in that book; thus I do =
not=20
      include any new graphics and GUI features or new enterprise =
features.=20
      Those are the subjects of <A=20
      href=3D"http://www.oreilly.com/catalog/jfcnut/"><I>Java Foundation =
Classes=20
      in a Nutshell</I></A> and <A=20
      href=3D"http://www.oreilly.com/catalog/jentnut/"><I>Java =
Enterprise in a=20
      Nutshell</I></A>.</P>
      <P>
      <TABLE cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D8 width=3D336 align=3Dright =
border=3D0>
